Changes are local only; do not push until the user asks.

## Latest run UI and stronger snare

The latest supplied beanstalk (2).png is preserved as player-stem-v3-source.png;
player-stem-v3.png is its transparent-background game adaptation. The road, menu
vines and cinematic use this version, with earlier versions retained for comparison.

The run HUD now uses two side columns: score, tale objective, letters, powers and
clue/status popups on the left; opponent status, aiming and the next obstacle on
the right. A soft mist fades the upper edge of the climb. There are no volume
controls or M shortcut; audio unlocks at a fixed mix level after interaction.
Keyboard/control banners, visible Pause control, obstacle advice, item instruction
labels and scrolling stage gates are removed from active gameplay. Esc still
pauses and opens the pause screen. Menus/practice retain their instructions.

Mud and sap now cause a real snare: lane movement uses 30% spring responsiveness
and accepted dodges must be at least 550ms apart for the effect's duration. Jumps
remain available, and road speed remains unchanged. The Cinderella reward still
shortens the effect. A left-side SNARED countdown shows when normal movement will
return; expiry immediately restores normal consecutive dodges. Tests cover the
cooldown boundary and expiry. Changes remain local until the user requests a push.

Verification for this pass: 253 game tests plus 3 backend tests pass, as do
formatting, typecheck and production build. Browser review confirms no volume
control, no active-run control prompts, separated side columns, the top fog fade
and the latest supplied beanstalk. The webcam dock is constrained to the left
column during play, even if it was expanded before the run.
